-- title:
--   Exactly one residually zero root at a prime with q²∣ N
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $N \geq 1$ satisfy: no prime cube divides $N$. Let $M_g \mid N$ be nonzero and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project, i.e. $a_1(g)=1$, the $q$-coefficients are multiplicative on coprime indices and satisfy the usual prime-power recursions (with $p$-Euler factor dropped at primes dividing $M_g$), and no proper divisor $M \mid M_g$ carries a normalised eigenform agreeing with $g$ at all primes not dividing $M_g$. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb C$ from the Hecke algebra of level $M_g$, weight $2$ with empty excluded set (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the cusp forms generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M_g$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M_g$), assumed to send $T_\ell \mapsto a_\ell(g)$ and $U_q \mapsto a_q(g)$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ into an algebraic closure $\bar K$ of $\operatorname{Frac}\mathcal O$. Let $q \neq p$ be a prime with $q^2 \mid N$. Put $a_q = \iota\chi_g(U_q) \in \bar K$ if $q \mid M_g$ and $a_q = \iota\chi_g(T_q)$ otherwise, set $e = v_q(N) - v_q(M_g)$, and let $P = X - a_q$ if $e = 0$ and $P = X^{e-1}\bigl(X^2 - a_q X + \epsilon\bigr)$ otherwise, where $\epsilon = 0$ if $q \mid M_g$ and $\epsilon = q$ if not. Then the sum, over the distinct roots $x$ of $P$ in $\bar K$ that are residually zero — meaning that $x$ is a root of some monic $R \in \mathcal O[X]$ whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ is $X^{\deg R}$ — of the multiplicity of $x$ as a root of $P$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the local root count at a prime $q$ exactly dividing $N$ to the second power: the local polynomial attached to $g$ at $q$ has, counted with multiplicity, exactly one root that is residually zero. It feeds the computation of the multiplicity with which a newform contributes to the residually-$0$ generalised eigenspace of $U_q$ in a corner realisation, used in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self).
